{{also|obst}}
==German==

===Etymology===
* From {{inh|de|gmh|obez}}, from {{inh|de|goh|obez}}, {{m|goh|obaz||fruit}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*ubatją|t=fruit, produce, increase}}, from a compound whose first element represents {{der|de|ine-pro|*obʰi-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ebʰi-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*bʰi-|t=on, toward, from, by}}, and whose second element is {{der|de|gem-pro|*at}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ēta-|t=edibles, food}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*etaną||t=to eat}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*h₁ed-|t=to eat}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|ovest|t=mast}}, {{cog|gml|ōvet}}, {{m|gml|āvet}}, {{m|gml|ōft||t=fruit}}, {{cog|nds-de|Aaft||fruits}}, {{cog|nl|ooft||fruits}}. More at {{l|en|ovest}}.
* The drug sense likely derives from cocaine being smuggled through ports in fruit crates.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=de|/oːpst/}}
* {{audio|De-Obst.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

